{"ts": "2026-08-17T11:08:40Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 116, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "72effca Stop the e2e harness orphaning its dev servers\n---\ncommit 72effca8a3dc0a92c834fe8fdb46b40164d126da\nAuthor: test-project <dev@test-project.local>\nDate:   Mon Aug 17 09:55:50 2026 +0000\n\n    Stop the e2e harness orphaning its dev servers\n    \n    Each e2e run leaked a vite process. terminate() killed the process we spawned,\n    but `npm run dev` is a wrapper and its vite child survived as an orphan, so\n    every run left one behind: nineteen had accumulated, holding roughly 1.4 GB on\n    a 4 GB container.\n    \n    Both servers now start with start_new_session=True, which puts each in its own\n    process group, and teardown signals the whole group -- SIGTERM, then SIGKILL if\n    it does not go quietly -- rather than only the direct child.\n    \n    Verified by counting vite and uvicorn processes either side of a full run:\n    zero before, zero after, 20/20 still passing.\n\n e2e/conftest.py | 33 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------\n 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_012eeezDL1vX1bZJ8iEDizvW", "session_id": "f5bbe20f-00f0-44c5-8e27-0f0d28f060fa"}}
